# Production Deploy Target Rule

- This repository's production deployment target is `training-system-seven` on Vercel under scope `mikhails-projects-de0149d2`.
- When the user asks to "commit/push and redeploy production", deploy from current `main` to this target.
- Preferred deploy command:
  - `npx vercel --prod --yes --scope mikhails-projects-de0149d2 --name training-system-seven`
- Mandatory redeploy checklist (do not skip steps):
  1. Commit and push requested changes to `main`.
  2. Run production deploy command above.
  3. Capture deploy outputs: deployment URL and inspector URL.
  4. Verify prod alias target:
     - `npx vercel inspect training-system-seven.vercel.app --scope mikhails-projects-de0149d2`
     - Confirm it resolves to the latest deployment id/url.
  5. If alias is stale, fix it immediately:
     - `npx vercel alias set <latest-deployment-url> training-system-seven.vercel.app --scope mikhails-projects-de0149d2`
  6. Re-check `training-system-seven.vercel.app` after alias update and confirm it points to latest.
- If user reports old prod UI, check for legacy URL usage first (for example `training-system.vercel.app`) and then verify alias mapping as above.
- Always report back:
  - Production URL: `https://training-system-seven.vercel.app`
  - Latest deployment URL (from deploy output)
  - Inspector URL (from deploy output)
  - Whether alias correction was needed
